Usage: ms <command> [arguments] [options]
       ms help [command]

Manuscript checks, builds, and runs .ms source and ms.toml projects.

Commands:
  check          Check types, formatting, and lint rules; --only picks one, --test adds the tests
  fmt            Format source files or a project
  build          Build a native executable, or emit its intermediate code with --emit
  run            Build and run an application; --profile captures a sampling profile
  test           Execute test blocks, including imported modules
  bench          Run and time bench blocks, including imported modules
  map            Show a program's structure: call graph views, a project review, checked metadata
  init           Create a new project with a manifest, entry, test, .gitignore, and .gitattributes
  install        Download the packages under [dependencies] and pin them in ms.lock
  add            Add a git dependency to ms.toml and install it
  remove         Remove a dependency from ms.toml and ms.lock
  search         Find a project or standard-library symbol: definition, type, uses
  lsp            Serve the language server on stdin/stdout
  help           Show help for a command, or explain a diagnostic code
  dev            Tools for working on Manuscript itself

Options:
  -h, --help  Show help
  --version   Print the compiler version

Native build levels:
  --build-type <Debug|Release|MinSizeRel>
  Default: Release

Start with:
  ms init hello
  ms check
  ms run ms.toml -- first second

Inside a project directory, commands that take a target default to ./ms.toml:
  ms run -- first second

Bare ms prints this help and exits successfully.
Long options that take values also accept --flag=value.
Run 'ms help <command>' or 'ms <command> --help' for usage and examples.
Builds link with the linker bundled in ms on every platform; no C compiler or SDK is needed.
MANUSCRIPT_CACHE_DIR selects the user cache for standalone run/test/profile artifacts.
